          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Seizure onset occurred at 8 years of age. The epilepsy is drug-responsive and has a structural etiology. MRI demonstrates a vascular malformation.\n\nCurrent Medications:\n- Valproate, current antiseizure medication.\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately 2 focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures per month.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, associated with a structural etiology and MRI evidence of a vascular malformation.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue valproate.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency.\n- Follow up in the epilepsy clinic.",
